<<<
compare smells strong or delicious (i.e. has a strong or delicious smell) with smells strongly or suspiciously of whisky or deliciously of violets; & (b) when to smell is used, as it may be, for to stink, an adverb is the right addition—this water smells outrageously;
===
compare *smells strong or delicious* (i.e. has a strong or delicious smell) with *smells strongly or suspiciously of whisky or deliciously of violets*; & (b) when *to smell* is used, as it may be, for *to stink*, an adverb is the right addition—*this water smells outrageously*;
