<<<
2. So long, & so to —, do so. Se long used colloquially for goodbye ox ' au revoir. It perhaps matters little for practical purposes, but the OKI? | gives no countenance to the deriva- tion from salaam, & treats the: phrase as a mere special combina- tion of so & long;
